[center][size=6][b]Colors+[/b][/size]
[size=4]Custom Color Picker for Star Wars: Zero Company[/size][/center]

Tired of picking from the same handful of swatches? [b]Colors+[/b] lets you choose [b]any color you like[/b] for your characters and your blasters.

Look for the new [b]CUSTOM COLOR[/b] button under the color choices. It opens a color picker where you can drag to any shade or type in a color code, and you see the result on your character or weapon as you go.

[line]
[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Any color, live.[/b] A color box, a rainbow bar and a color-code box, with a live preview on your character or weapon.
[*][b]Main-menu character creator and the barracks.[/b] Clothing and armor, hair, skin (including species skin tones, such as Zabrak), makeup, tattoos, horns and scars.
[*][b]Armory blaster paint.[/b] Give your blasters a custom Paint Color, and try it on every Location and Paint Finish before you commit.
[*][b]Apply or Cancel.[/b] Nothing changes until you apply; Cancel puts your old color back.
[*][b]Saved like any other color.[/b] Your colors are stored by the game itself, so they stay put after loading a save, and even if you remove the mod.
[*][b]Plays nice with unlocker mods.[/b] Armor wearing a color the palette no longer offers can still be changed.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]UE4SS for Star Wars Zero Company[/b] (see the Requirements tab). Both mod managers below can install it for you.
[/list]
No other mods are needed.

[line]
[size=5][b]Installing[/b][/size]

[b]With Zero Company Mod Command[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Make sure UE4SS is installed: Mod Command shows its status on the Settings card. If it isn't, follow the card's offer to install the Nexus build.
[*]Open the [b]Hangar Bay[/b] and drag the Colors+ ZIP anywhere into the window.
[*]Check that Colors+ is switched on in the Hangar Bay, then start the game with [b]LAUNCH GAME[/b].
[/list]

[b]With Zero Mod Manager[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Make sure UE4SS is installed: go to [b]Home → Runtime readiness → UE4SS runtime[/b] if it isn't.
[*]Download the Colors+ ZIP, open [b]Install[/b] and drop the ZIP into the app. Look over the summary and click [b]Install[/b].
[*]Check that Colors+ is switched on in [b]Mods[/b], then start the game.
[/list]

[b]By hand[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Close the game.
[*]Open the ZIP and drag the [b]ColorsPlus[/b] folder into your game's UE4SS mods folder:
[code]SWZeroCompany/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/[/code]
[*]Start the game.
[/list]

[b]Updating:[/b] close the game first. With a mod manager, install the new ZIP the same way. By hand, copy the new [b]ColorsPlus[/b] folder over your old one. Only one copy of Colors+ can be installed at a time.

[line]
[size=5][b]How to use it[/b][/size]

Click [b]CUSTOM COLOR[/b] under a color choice. Drag in the color box and along the rainbow bar, or type a color code. [b]APPLY COLOR[/b] keeps your new color; [b]CANCEL[/b] puts the old one back.

[list]
[*][b]Main-menu creator:[/b] save your character as usual to keep your colors. If you leave without saving, your old colors come back.
[*][b]Barracks:[/b] your colors are kept as soon as you apply them, and saved with your game.
[*][b]Armory → Customize Weapon:[/b] while the picker is open you're only previewing, so feel free to try different Locations and Paint Finishes to see how your color looks on each. [b]APPLY COLOR[/b] paints the weapon for real.
[/list]

Want one of the game's own colors back? Just click its swatch.

[line]
[size=5][b]Uninstalling[/b][/size]

Switch Colors+ off or remove it in your mod manager, or delete the [b]ColorsPlus[/b] folder. Your custom colors stay on your characters and weapons, and your saves load fine without the mod.

[line]
[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/291]MinervaMagicka's Character Overhaul Suite[/url]: compatible.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/34]Smexy's ZCUnlocked[/url]: mostly compatible. Custom colors don't work for its Blaster Bolt or Lightsaber colors.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/134]Coppershore's Ship Paint and Hangar Lift[/url]: not tested yet.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Known issues[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Mouse only: the buttons can't be reached with a controller.
[*]Eye colors aren't supported (eye-color options added by another mod may be).
[*]Restart the game after installing or updating Colors+. Don't use UE4SS's "Reload All Mods"; it can crash or freeze the game.
[*]Sweeping the mouse quickly across the color swatches can close the picker. Your previous color is kept; just open it again.
[*]The picker's buttons are in English only for now.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Found a problem?[/b][/size]

Post in the Bugs tab and let us know what you were customizing (which character or weapon), what happened, and which other mods you use. It helps a lot if you attach these two files from the [b]ColorsPlus[/b] folder:

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]colors_plus_probe.log[/font]
[*][font=Courier New]colors_plus_performance.log[/font]
[/list]

They only contain technical details about what the mod did: no screenshots, saves or personal files. They may mention folder paths on your PC, so feel free to look them over before sending.
